{"event_type":"review","id":"96ff96e727786176a6116a2d449332ce18e5d32eb767032aec8688397da77319","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T09:31:32Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7aaa51adc9d7a274c4dca9d609f30616d63061df7be2a4aa30e4cac217727694","sha256":"7aaa51adc9d7a274c4dca9d609f30616d63061df7be2a4aa30e4cac217727694"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0163e97181105ccfc9f7d358749b908bf51e08b60134fc2faee031750055f86f","sha256":"0163e97181105ccfc9f7d358749b908bf51e08b60134fc2faee031750055f86f"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/efb1ef0a0ff21f4e53b51625d13137b8e81927618636029a640b505dbb3a335f","sha256":"efb1ef0a0ff21f4e53b51625d13137b8e81927618636029a640b505dbb3a335f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/67e8fa59d27380b632995ace0a240d8be008bde6adaa801205bc1f8de48d281d","sha256":"67e8fa59d27380b632995ace0a240d8be008bde6adaa801205bc1f8de48d281d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1362327131b47f8b4b14d38c73deb0573ee49500c835eff4bc2533ad01256230","sha256":"1362327131b47f8b4b14d38c73deb0573ee49500c835eff4bc2533ad01256230"}],"attempt_id":"533629157bb95adb02a34756bdd8201857a8461a1fcf61d12a55fdcefcff870e:0:1","base":"54066cd591129f205b330c76c15fae5e88c7df7c","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"687a9af794ed0dff4cb7aef53e0281250d2fc8d0","body":"**The evidence gate accepts `line` values of 0 or below.**\n\nAt `src/plans/review-loop.ts:831`, the only check is `line > lines.length`. A `FixEvidence` with `line: 0`, a negative value, or a non-integer passes for any blob that exists. It even passes for an empty file, where `lines.length === 0`. In that case `unchanged_with_reason` posts a stamped reply. On the next run, `loopReplyVerdict` treats the thread as settled. The worker's output then bypasses the gate that lines 1680-1685 describe as its protection: \"an unverified reason is no outcome\".\n\nSomething upstream in `fixReviewItem` may already reject `line < 1`, but nothing visible in this file does. The gate should reject these values itself, because it is the publication boundary.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   for (const { path, line } of evidence) {\n+    if (!Number.isSafeInteger(line) || line < 1) {\n+      return `${path}:${String(line)} is not a valid 1-based line`;\n+    }\n     // A FILE, not a tree: `git show <tip>:<dir>` succeeds on a directory too.\n```\n</details>","id":"85d04c1f9a0293e032822df357773f64f18807a325d341e5380ce908d3e9ba7b","intervals":[],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"The evidence gate accepts `line` values of 0 or below."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"687a9af794ed0dff4cb7aef53e0281250d2fc8d0","body":"**With `publish: false`, carried resolves are dropped and the run still reports `ok`.**\n\nLine 1776 skips `replyAndResolve` when `opts.publish === false`. The settle gate at lines 1119-1127 still pushes a pending resolve into `carriedResolves` and records the thread as `loop-replied-this-head`. Fix-row replies get a reason because of the `!publishable` branch at line 1643, but carried resolves get none.\n\nExample: a run has no fix jobs and one carried resolve. `reasons` stays empty, so `status` is `'ok'`, but the pending resolve was never sent. The `parent cancelled` path records its own reason at lines 1808-1809. The publish-disabled path should do the same.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   let reply: ReplyAndResolveResult | undefined;\n+  if (actions.length > 0 && opts.publish === false) {\n+    reasons.push(\n+      `${String(actions.length)} reply/resolve action(s) withheld; publication requires --push`,\n+    );\n+  }\n   if (actions.length > 0 && !opts.signal?.aborted && opts.publish !== false) {\n```\n</details>","id":"746958e71d18ceae5a8b4b44d1c9ec20e8c57ce2d9f81d4010d44c19b2b3eb44","intervals":[],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"With `publish: false`, carried resolves are dropped and the run still reports `ok`."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"687a9af794ed0dff4cb7aef53e0281250d2fc8d0","body":"**Include `reasoning` in the token fold.**\n\nWhen usage includes `reasoning`, `onSpend` underreports tokens. The sweep also deducts too little at `src/selfhost/self-review-loop.ts:689`, so it can dispatch more work after exhausting its token budget.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  usage === undefined ? 0 : usage.input + usage.output + usage.cacheRead + usage.cacheWrite;\n+  usage === undefined\n+    ? 0\n+    : usage.input + usage.output + usage.cacheRead + usage.cacheWrite + (usage.reasoning ?? 0);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"d8df0dabafb63ba93429018cbadfedce808280820c3164736343b1cdc149d0be","intervals":[],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Include `reasoning` in the token fold."}],"head":"146888b9b9055a0c5251b208ad60991d6cd0f4e7","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"687a9af794ed0dff4cb7aef53e0281250d2fc8d0","intervals":[[9,9],[12,15],[76,82],[100,102],[108,109],[112,113],[115,116],[118,120],[156,311],[371,372],[381,383],[411,416],[472,492],[495,497],[502,517],[522,523],[576,583],[691,694],[788,837],[930,936],[940,960],[969,1017],[1060,1136],[1157,1162],[1166,1168],[1184,1186],[1188,1282],[1284,1284],[1315,1315],[1325,1325],[1332,1347],[1520,1530],[1533,1540],[1543,1545],[1547,1551],[1559,1563],[1567,1576],[1586,1586],[1649,1655],[1657,1701],[1703,1703],[1762,1763],[1776,1776],[1788,1788],[1808,1809]],"path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts"},{"blob":"593f1129b94747902854507c4b6ed503a9c0474c","intervals":[[17,18],[22,43],[71,83],[86,91],[94,101],[247,250],[252,265],[304,305],[308,383],[425,428],[512,520],[523,534],[548,555],[573,573],[632,632],[642,642],[649,650],[667,667],[669,669],[686,687],[689,696],[705,706],[708,711],[715,717],[725,851],[856,869],[871,885],[887,934],[938,938],[943,1017]],"path":"src/selfhost/self-review-loop.ts"},{"blob":"0f074003455c62c5dee7dd4757f134fafd8a8a21","intervals":[[2,5],[7,7],[22,37],[49,97]],"path":"test/global-setup.test.ts"},{"blob":"b6f2fcd734e1c45dd5f565ae2a29996325c0f6d6","intervals":[[8,9],[14,19],[22,35],[41,41],[56,60],[69,69],[74,177],[199,257]],"path":"test/selfhost/config.test.ts"}],"job_id":"533629157bb95adb02a34756bdd8201857a8461a1fcf61d12a55fdcefcff870e:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"b654976307e26f6499edd58293d4cc991e81b9fc","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/selfhost/self-review-loop.ts"},"merge":"d8da1e2f8a592f1858a1bf97cb04a729ce9f6d3b","method":"pre-merge","pre":"34401d741bd653d722472f4e99a1dca6040433ce","source_path":"src/selfhost/self-review-loop.ts"},"blob":"593f1129b94747902854507c4b6ed503a9c0474c","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/selfhost/self-review-loop.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"9b31ba3acf99de9a4af89266ca59348aebacaace","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts"},"merge":"d8da1e2f8a592f1858a1bf97cb04a729ce9f6d3b","method":"pre-merge","pre":"34401d741bd653d722472f4e99a1dca6040433ce","source_path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts"},"blob":"687a9af794ed0dff4cb7aef53e0281250d2fc8d0","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/plans/review-loop.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"c97691f64d8232c91a5550b7b6ea118d663cd9fe","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"test/global-setup.test.ts"},"merge":"d8da1e2f8a592f1858a1bf97cb04a729ce9f6d3b","method":"pre-merge","pre":"34401d741bd653d722472f4e99a1dca6040433ce","source_path":"test/global-setup.test.ts"},"blob":"0f074003455c62c5dee7dd4757f13